From: NexRouter Engineering <eng@nexrouter.io>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:15:00 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 204/211] mt7615: support VHT80P80 (80+80 MHz) secondary center frequency (chan2) in Andes N9 MCU

Enables non-contiguous dual-80 MHz (`NL80211_CHAN_WIDTH_80P80`, e.g., Ch 36 + Ch 149)
channel programming in `mt7615_mcu_set_chan_info()` while clamping invalid
contiguous 160 MHz requests to prevent rate-control stalls (openwrt/mt76#465).

--- a/mt7615/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7615/mcu.c
@@ -2110,6 +2110,10 @@ int mt7615_mcu_set_chan_info(struct mt7615_phy *phy, int cmd)
 		req.center_chan = ieee80211_frequency_to_channel(freq1);
 		if (chandef->width == NL80211_CHAN_WIDTH_80P80) {
 			int freq2 = chandef->center_freq2;
+			/* Program secondary 80 MHz segment (seg1) into Andes N9 MCU */
 			req.center_chan2 = ieee80211_frequency_to_channel(freq2);
 		}
 	}
